name 'iterating-with-ai-preassessment-q6_2025'

question 'If an app tries to render an array of data that is currently empty, what is a "Human-Centered Design" best practice?'

wrong 'Show a blank white screen so the user isn\'t distracted.'
right 'Show an "empty state" message (e.g., "No items found") to provide transparency and build trust.'
wrong 'Automatically generate random data so the screen isn\'t empty.'
wrong 'Trigger an error message that tells the user the code is broken.'

allow_multiple_attempts false

teacher_markdown <<MARKDOWN
Lesson 4

Providing an empty state or a count of 0 results is more transparent. It informs the user that the system is working correctly but simply has no data to show at the moment.
MARKDOWN
